        "original_id": "7589d9c5-9764-5e82-b7b6-c1375d011368",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fredric March, Charles Laughton, Elsa Lanchester, Frances Drake, Victor Hugo, Martha Scott, Beulah Bondi, Gene Lockhart, Elisabeth Fraser\n- Works: Les Misérables (1935 film), One Foot in Heaven\n- Roles: Eponine\n\nFacts:\n- In 1927, Charles Laughton was cast in a play with his future wife Elsa Lanchester, and they lived and worked together until his death; they had no children.\n- Les Misérables is a 1935 American drama film based on Victor Hugo's novel of the same name and starring Fredric March and Charles Laughton.\n- Frances Drake was an American actress born on October 22, 1912, and she was best known for playing Eponine in Les Misérables (1935).\n- One Foot in Heaven is a 1941 American biographical film starring Fredric March, Martha Scott, Beulah Bondi, Gene Lockhart, and Elisabeth Fraser.\n- Frances Drake died on January 18, 2000.",
